  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one.\n\nFor an open bound (`min_open` or `max_open`), the clamped value was moved the wrong way. With `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)`, an input of `-5` clamped to `-1`, which is outside the range. The first valid integer is `1`. The same mistake affected `max_open`. The line was `bound - dir` and is now `bound + dir`.\n\nClosed bounds were already correct. `FloatRange` can't hit this, because it rejects clamping with open bounds.",
